opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Fine-grained reactive web interfaces for OCaml, with pluggable JS backends"
description: """
Reativa builds reactive browser interfaces in OCaml. Its fine-grained reactive
core provides Signal, Computed, Effect and a glitch-free scheduler, while the
View layer mounts real DOM nodes and updates reactive text, attributes and
dynamic regions in place — no virtual DOM.

The browser FFI lives behind two dune virtual modules (Dom and History). This
package ships the core, the mlx JSX ppx, and the Melange backend as the default
implementation, so (libraries reativa) compiles to JavaScript with Melange.

To use js_of_ocaml instead, install the reativa-jsoo package and name it
alongside this one: (libraries reativa reativa-jsoo).
"""
maintainer: "Bernardo Gurgel <brnrdog@hey.com>"
authors: "Bernardo Gurgel <brnrdog@hey.com>"
license: "MIT"
homepage: "https://github.com/brnrdog/reativa"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/brnrdog/reativa/issues"
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/brnrdog/reativa.git"
depends: [
  "ocaml" {>= "4.14"}
  "dune" {>= "3.16"}
  "melange" {>= "3.0.0"}
  "mlx"
  "ppxlib"
  "ocamlmerlin-mlx" {with-dev-setup}
]
build: [
  ["dune" "build" "-p" name "-j" jobs "@install" "@runtest" {with-test}]
]
